# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# This file exists because of a concrete, silent failure: the world builder
# computes a `sourceHash` by hashing the raw bytes of
# maps/art-world-v2.layout.json and maps/art-world-v2.obstacles.json. With
# core.autocrlf=true those files are CRLF in a Windows working tree and LF in a
# Linux one, so the hash differs by platform and the builder's staleness guard
# rejects a world that is in fact current.
#
# The practical effect was that the world could only be built on the machine
# that generated the collision review. CI on Linux failed with
# "Stale collision review" on a tree that built perfectly on Windows.
#
# Declaring these as LF makes the hashed bytes identical everywhere.

# Any file whose bytes are hashed, or that is executed on Linux, must be LF.
maps/*.json           text eol=lf
tools/*.mjs           text eol=lf
tools/*.mts           text eol=lf
deploy/azure/*.sh     text eol=lf
*.yml                 text eol=lf
*.yaml                text eol=lf

# Source and docs: normalised in the repository, checked out natively.
*.ts    text
*.js    text
*.mjs   text
*.mts   text
*.json  text
*.css   text
*.html  text
*.md    text

# Binary assets must never be transformed. The artwork is hashed too, so a
# single altered byte would invalidate the collision review.
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.db    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pem   binary
